note as N1
  Font loading
  - The default font is loaded from the project assets folder: DEFAULT_FONT_PATH (adjust to the real file name in /assets/fonts).
    It is embedded with include_bytes! in release builds so the executable is self-contained.
  - The font is rasterised by fontdue at the pixel height that makes the glyph box fit cell_w x cell_h (8 x 15).
    mask(ch) returns an alpha mask of EXACTLY cell_w * cell_h bytes: the glyph is placed on the baseline, clipped to the cell.
  - If the font has no glyph for ch, mask() returns the mask of '?' and contains() returns false.
  - If the asset is a BITMAP font (BDF / PSF) replace TtfGlyphSource by another GlyphSource implementation;
    nothing else in the design changes (everything depends on the GlyphSource trait only).
end note

note as N2
  render() - exact compositing (see activity diagram 20)
  - Output size = canvas.pixel_width x canvas.pixel_height (1920 x 1080 for the default canvas), RGBA8, alpha always 255.
  - pixel = frame.background; if cell.bg = Some(c) pixel = c; then pixel = lerp(pixel, cell.fg, mask_alpha / 255).
  ThumbnailBuilder::build(frame): ONE pixel per cell (cols x rows image):
    base = cell.bg or frame.background;  if glyph != ' ' pixel = lerp(base, cell.fg, 0.6) else pixel = base.
end note

note as N3
  wrap(kind, payload): header.magic = kind.magic(), version = 1, uncompressed_len = payload.len(), crc32 = crc32fast(payload),
  payload is compressed with zstd level 3 and flags bit0 = 1 (stored_len = compressed length).
  If compression does not make it smaller, store raw with flags bit0 = 0 (stored_len = uncompressed_len).
  unwrap(kind, bytes): see decode activity diagram (20). Binary layouts: diagram 08.
end note

note as N4
  save(path, project): bytes = AsprCodec.encode(project); AtomicWriter::write(path, bytes).
  load(path): read whole file -> AsprCodec.decode. io NotFound -> RepoError::NotFound.
  The caller (AsciiPaintApp) is responsible for project.touch_modified(now) before save and for history.mark_clean() after success.
end note

note as N5
  write(path, bytes): 1) tmp = path + ".tmp" in the same directory  2) write all bytes, flush, File::sync_all()
  3) fs::rename(tmp, path) (atomic replace on the same volume)  4) on ANY error remove tmp and return the error.
  A crash therefore leaves either the old file or the new file, never a half-written one.
end note

note as N6
  - Stored as JSON { "version": 1, "entries": [ {"name", "path", "last_opened_unix"} ] } in <config_dir>/AsciiPaint/recent.json
    (dirs::config_dir()). Missing / corrupt file -> empty list (a corrupt file is renamed recent.json.bad, never a crash).
  - touch(): remove an existing entry with the same path, insert at index 0, truncate to MAX_ENTRIES, persist().
  - entries() is always sorted by last_opened_unix descending (guaranteed by touch()).
  - Called on: project created, project opened, Save As to a new .aspr path.
end note

note as N7
  PNG       : buf = FrameRasterizer::render(selected frame); image crate encodes RGBA8 PNG; AtomicWriter.
  .ascii    : AsciiCodec.encode(AsciiImage{ canvas, font_name, frame = selected frame clone }); AtomicWriter.
  .aanim    : AanimCodec.encode(AsciiAnimation{ canvas, font_name, fps, looping, frames = all frames }); AtomicWriter.
  MP4       : start_mp4() clones the frames into Mp4Worker and spawns ONE std::thread; returns immediately.
  PNG / .ascii / .aanim run synchronously on the UI thread (small, fast). Only MP4 is asynchronous.
end note

note as N8
  run():
  1. spawn  ffmpeg -y -hide_banner -loglevel error -f rawvideo -pix_fmt rgba -s {W}x{H} -framerate {fps} -i pipe:0
            -vf pad=ceil(iw/2)*2:ceil(ih/2)*2 -c:v libx264 -preset medium -crf 18 -pix_fmt yuv420p -movflags +faststart
            -f mp4 {out}.part      (stdin piped, stderr piped; no shell is used, each token is one argument)
  2. a helper thread drains stderr into a ring buffer of the last 4 KiB (prevents a full pipe from blocking ffmpeg).
  3. for i in 0..frames.len(): if cancel is set -> kill child, delete {out}.part, send Cancelled, return.
       buf = FrameRasterizer::render(frames[i]); stdin.write_all(&buf.pixels); send Progress(i + 1, total).
  4. drop(stdin); status = child.wait(). status != 0 -> delete .part, send Failed(FfmpegFailed(code, stderr_tail)).
  5. fs::rename({out}.part, {out}); send Finished(out).
  Any io error on the pipe -> kill child, delete .part, send Failed(Io).
end note

note as N9
  find(): 1) <exe dir>/ffmpeg(.exe)  2) search every directory in PATH for ffmpeg(.exe).  Returns the first executable found.
  Evaluated once at startup and again each time the Save modal opens (so installing ffmpeg does not need a restart).
end note


